  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready: six items on O4, \"Workflows or agents: who owns the control flow?\". The quiz is in `quizzes/0002.json` and the key in `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **q1:** short answer, about who decides the next step in a workflow.\n- **q2, q3, q5, q6:** multiple choice. They cover spotting a workflow, why a fixed workflow suits known steps, correcting the \"tools means agent\" idea, and splitting the makerspace assistant into agent and workflow parts.\n- **q4:** a numeric item that compares the model calls an agent makes with a workflow's fixed count. It builds on the loop you already know from quiz 0001.\n\nThe quiz is ahead of the lessons, because there is no lesson on O4 yet. I wrote it from the standard definition: a workflow's code paths are fixed in advance, and in an agent the model directs its own steps. I did not search for a source this time. I also did not tag any wrong options with misconception ids, because none of the existing ids clearly matched.\n\nDo you want a short lesson on O4 before you take it? If so, tell me how many minutes.",
